No.  Change line 366 of fountain.c from:

		if (u.ualign.type != A_LAWFUL) {

to:

		if (u.ualign.type != A_LAWFUL || !Role_if(PM_KNIGHT)) {
	
> Would anyone actually be against a free, decent and easy artifact for every 
> lawful character since there really aren't free and easy artifacts for 
> chaotics or neutrals especially if the latter two are following atheist 
> conduct.

That's exactly why I made the change, because there isn't much reason
for a lawful to bother getting any other weapon in vanilla.  Excalibur
isn't "the best" lawful weapon, of course, and some classes won't even
have the longsword skill until one of the n-1 billion longsword
artifacts gets gifted to them, but even with those restrictions it's
more than enough to ascend with, and given its ease of obtainment it's
basically a no-brainer for any Lawful.

Why is this bad?  Because, like SDSM and GDSM, it's so far past the rest
of the comparable artifacts on the scale that it removes any sort of
meaningful choice from the game.  Sure, you can waste time masturbating over
an altar until you get Grayswandir if you're fixated on numbers, or you can
insist on using Demonbane or something, but most of that just falls into
the category of "look, I can win with one hand tied behind my back";
amusing, but not something that should be required for a player just to
add some variety to things.

